5. What is Endpoint Security?

An endpoint device refers to a computer or a workstation, which can be threatened by various cyber security attacks. Moreover, the endpoint device is commonly the weakest link in networks and cyber security systems in general. Endpoint security aims to protect these devices from being hacked, compromised, or infected with malicious software that may steal or damage data or files.

The main concept is as follows:

endpoint monitoring → threat detection → alert → investigation → response

6. What is Microsoft Defender?

Microsoft Defender is an anti-virus software that scans files, applications, and other activity on the computer to detect threats. It includes such features as real-time protection, malware scans, threat detection, and quarantine of malicious software. Thus, Microsoft Defender is important because it helps protect Windows devices without making the user conduct regular scans of every file they open.

7. Windows Security

Windows Security is the program which allows one to operate the security functions. It consists of multiple components such as:

Virus & threat protection: where one can check the status of the antivirus and perform scans;

Firewall & network protection: the status of firewall and network protection is examined;

App & browser control: protection from malicious apps, software, and websites;

Device security: information about security features on a device;

Device performance & health: information about the general performance and health of the device running on Windows.

8. Real-Time Protection

Real-time Protection is an important feature of Microsoft Defender. It ensures the scanning of files, programs, and other activities when the computer is operating. The program detects threats in real-time and warns the user and blocks malicious activity. 

9. Security Scanning

Windows Defender offers multiple scanning options for checking the computer for threats.

Quick Scan: it is the fastest type of scan which analyzes the most common locations where threats are detected;

Full Scan: it is a complete scan of the computer which may take more time;

Custom Scan: when using this option, one can specify the desired files or locations to be scanned.

In the current practical, Quick Scan will be used to evaluate the current status of the computer.

10. Protection History

Protection History is the section where one can see the details of the security scanning, such as detected threats, blocked files, and potentially unwanted applications. It is important to check it to see if any security threats were detected by the system.

11. Windows Defender Firewall

Windows Defender Firewall is a security feature that monitors and controls network traffic in bound and out bound on the computer to ensure that unauthorized users are not accessing the computer. 

12. PowerShell Monitoring

PowerShell is a scripting module in Windows which allows one to perform certain actions on the computer. The following command can be used to check the status of Defender:

Get-MpComputerStatus

After entering this command, the status of the Microsoft Defender services will pop up on the screen, indicating whether everything is operating normally.

13. Endpoint Security Monitoring Workflow

Windows Computer → Windows Security → Microsoft Defender → Security Monitoring → Threat Detection → Security Alert → Investigation → Response / Protection

The current workflow demonstrates how threat detection works on a Windows machine. After installing Microsoft Defender as a part of Windows Security, one can check the status, run a scan, and detect any malicious software. 

14. Importance of Endpoint Security Monitoring

Various endpoints are regularly under attack, and thus, it is necessary to ensure that they are secured. Monitoring of the computer allows:

1.Detecting malware and other threats;

1.Checking if antivirus is working

2.Detecting any threats which might appear in the network

3.Monitoring of firewall

4.Securing important files and data

5.Responding to detected threats;

6.Enhancing the protection of the computer.

15. Advantages of Microsoft Defender

The main advantages of Microsoft Defender include:

1.It is embedded into Windows Operating System;

2.It provides real-time protection

3.Has various scanning options

4.Detects malware and other threats

Offers firewall and network protection
Has Protection History which detects all the threats;

PowerShell status check;

Provides a basic set of protection without a need to install additional antivirus software.

16. Limitations

Microsoft Defender is a great tool; however, there are some limitations to it. First of all, no antivirus software can offer absolute protection from any threats.  In addition, enterprises and other organizations may experience greater levels of security threats, and thus, having Microsoft Defender may not be sufficient.

